  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "The first step in finding the product \\((3x+2)(x-5)\\) by use of the distributive property in the form \\(a(b+c)=ab+ac\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3x^2-13x-10\\)",
    "B": "\\(3x(x-5)+2(x-5)\\)",
    "C": "\\((3x+2)x+(3x+2)(-5)\\)",
    "D": "\\(3x^2-17x-10\\)",
    "E": "\\(3x^2+2x-15x-10\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The specified form \\(a(b+c)=ab+ac\\) keeps the first factor intact and distributes it over the two terms of the second factor. Write \\(x-5=x+(-5)\\), then take\n\\[\na=3x+2,\\qquad b=x,\\qquad c=-5.\n\\]\nThe first distribution step is therefore\n\\[\n(3x+2)x+(3x+2)(-5),\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
